<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    RDR-192 Step 7 (bead nexus-wbfpw.15): reapable(c), the ONE engine
    predicate for "this chunk is garbage collection's to take", as an
    inlinable SQL function. Non-destructive: this changeset creates the
    function and nothing else. Its first consumers are Step 8's
    gc_quarantine_orphans pair (vectors-022) and the read-only listing route;
    the periodic reaper (nexus-2x9xa) is the third.

    THE PREDICATE. A chunk row c is reapable when ALL of:

      1. c.last_written_at < now() - grace. last_written_at, not created_at
         (Sam, 2026-09-29, nexus-wbfpw.43): created_at is write-once, so a
         re-write would otherwise get no fresh grace. last_written_at is
         refreshed by every client write path and by no maintenance UPDATE
         (vectors-020's header carries the contract). The existence-partition
         metadata refresh (the have-vector branch of upsert-chunks and the
         identical-text branch of the combined write, both batchUpdateMetadata)
         IS one of those client write paths, so it bumps last_written_at.
      2. no catalog_document_chunks row names (tenant, collection, chash) in
         ANY owner state. A tombstoned owner still has a manifest row, so a
         chunk whose only owners are tombstoned is NOT reapable: it is
         purge_trash's, which ages the tombstone, not the chunk.
      3. no document in index_state 'indexing' names the chunk, until that
         run's index_started_at is older than the pin TTL. A multi-batch
         re-index replaces the manifest at batch 1, so every old tail chunk is
         ownerless until a later batch re-adds it (RDR-223 Phase 2 gate
         critique, S2). The pin is a document-level, TTL-bounded exclusion so a
         dead run cannot hold chunks forever. The chunk names its document by
         metadata catalog_doc_id, falling back to doc_id when that is absent or
         empty: the same forward key the manifest-less census uses. An
         'indexing' row with no index_started_at cannot be aged, so it does not
         pin (its TTL cannot be evaluated; the begin route always stamps it).

    PARAMETERS. p_grace and p_pin_ttl are intervals; NULL means the default
    (30 days and 7 days). The defaults live here and nowhere else, so a caller
    that passes NULL cannot drift from the predicate. Tests inject small
    values; a delete path must clamp a user-supplied grace to a floor before it
    reaches this function (the SQL stays pure).

    SHAPE. Same as live(c) (vectors-018): a set-returning function, because a
    scalar RETURNS boolean whose body holds an EXISTS subquery can never be
    inlined, and an opaque per-row call is what the .9 round-1 EXPLAIN caught.
    It returns one row when the chunk is reapable and none otherwise, so a
    caller writes:

        EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM nexus.chunk_is_reapable(
                    c.tenant_id, c.collection, c.chash, c.last_written_at,
                    c.metadata, NULL, NULL))

    The row's own last_written_at and metadata are PASSED IN rather than
    re-read, which is what lets the same call be the WHERE of a DELETE: after
    inlining, the grace comparison is a qual on the DELETE's own target row, so
    a client write that refreshes last_written_at while the DELETE waits on its
    row lock is seen when READ COMMITTED rechecks the new row version, and the
    DELETE skips it. A select-then-delete-by-key would not see it. The manifest
    and pin sub-queries are not rechecked by that mechanism: a manifest row
    committed during the DELETE is the sweep gate's concern (every destructive
    consumer takes it, as gc_quarantine_orphans and runSweepTransaction do), not
    this function's.

    THE PIN PROBE IS FENCED WITH OFFSET 0. Under FORCE RLS a NOSUPERUSER role
    such as nexus_svc evaluates a user qual below the policy's security barrier,
    and so can use it as an index condition, only when every function it calls is
    LEAKPROOF; jsonb ->> text is not (nexus-wbfpw.4 round 4, pinned by
    ManifestLessCensusNotesGuardIndexPlanShapeTest). Written inline as
    d.tumbler = COALESCE(NULLIF(p_metadata ->> ...)) the key expression made the
    planner skip catalog_documents_pk and probe idx_catalog_documents_index_state
    instead, a bitmap scan of every 'indexing' document of the tenant per
    candidate chunk (40 heap rows per probe on the measured fixture, 802 ms for a
    60,000-chunk delete). OFFSET 0 keeps the key a subquery output, so the join
    clause is d.tumbler = kk.k, a leakproof text equality, and the probe is a
    primary-key lookup (455 ms for the same delete, 5 ms for a LIMIT 300
    listing). ChunkIsReapablePlanIntegrationTest pins the plan under nexus_svc.

    NOT A VIEW JOIN, for the reason vectors-009 and vectors-018 give.
    LANGUAGE sql, STABLE, SECURITY INVOKER (FORCE RLS on the catalog tables stays
    the isolation boundary), no function-level SET, not STRICT; EXECUTE is the
    PUBLIC default, as for chunk_live_owners.

    NO INDEX is added for last_written_at. A btree on it would stop HOT updates
    for every client re-write of a chunk (nexus-wbfpw.43 review), and the
    candidate scan is already bounded by the (tenant_id, collection, chash)
    primary key prefix. The plan measured under nexus_svc is in
    ChunkIsReapablePlanIntegrationTest.

    OTHER PREDICATES. strandedChunkCount (purge_trash Step 1) does NOT move onto
    this function: it counts chunks that HAVE a manifest row whose owners are all
    aged tombstones, the complement of arm 2 above, so the two are disjoint by
    design and together make the dead set. purge_trash keeps its own deleted_at
    grace. RDR-192 Technical Design records the same decision.

    ROW TYPE. RETURNS TABLE adds one generated jOOQ record
    (ChunkIsReapableRecord); JooqRecordReflectionFeatureTest's count moves by +1.

    No DATA EFFECT: a function definition only; no row changes. Placed after
    vectors-020 and before the grants-nexus-svc.xml runAlways block (D0.1).
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="vectors-021-1" author="nexus-wbfpw.15">
        <comment>nexus.chunk_is_reapable(tenant, collection, chash, last_written_at, metadata, grace, pin_ttl): RDR-192 reapable(c) as an inlinable set-returning SQL function. One row when the chunk has no own-collection manifest row in any owner state, last_written_at is older than the grace (default 30 days) and no document in index_state indexing (younger than the pin TTL, default 7 days) names it; no row otherwise. No call site migrated here (Step 8).</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="false" stripComments="false">
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION nexus.chunk_is_reapable(
    p_tenant          text,
    p_collection      text,
    p_chash           bytea,
    p_last_written_at timestamptz,
    p_metadata        jsonb,
    p_grace           interval DEFAULT NULL,
    p_pin_ttl         interval DEFAULT NULL
) RETURNS TABLE(reapable boolean)
LANGUAGE sql
STABLE
SECURITY INVOKER
AS $$
    SELECT true
     WHERE p_last_written_at &lt; now() - COALESCE(p_grace, interval '30 days')
       AND NOT EXISTS (
             SELECT 1
               FROM nexus.catalog_document_chunks m
              WHERE m.tenant_id  = p_tenant
                AND m.collection = p_collection
                AND m.chash      = p_chash
           )
       AND NOT EXISTS (
             SELECT 1
               FROM (SELECT COALESCE(NULLIF(p_metadata ->> 'catalog_doc_id', ''),
                                     NULLIF(p_metadata ->> 'doc_id', '')) AS k
                     OFFSET 0) kk
               JOIN nexus.catalog_documents d
                 ON d.tenant_id = p_tenant AND d.tumbler = kk.k
              WHERE d.index_state = 'indexing'
                AND d.index_started_at &gt; now() - COALESCE(p_pin_ttl, interval '7 days')
           )
$$;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS nexus.chunk_is_reapable(text, text, bytea, timestamptz, jsonb, interval, interval);</sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
